# No deploys without permission

**Never deploy** anything for this project unless the owner explicitly asks in that message.

Forbidden without explicit permission:
- `firebase deploy` (any target: hosting, firestore:rules, storage, functions, etc.)
- Publishing to Firebase Hosting, App Hosting, or any production/staging URL
- Pushing release tags or triggering CI deploy pipelines
- Enabling/configuring cloud services that go live for end users

Allowed without asking:
- Local work: `npm run build`, `npm run dev`, `npm run lint`, `npm run preview`
- Editing `firestore.rules`, `storage.rules`, `firebase.json` in the repo only
- Preparing deploy commands for the owner to run themselves

If deploy seems needed, stop and wait for the owner to say so. Do not ask repeatedly — just do not deploy.
